<Base lang="en-US" pageType="CollectionPage" title="Read the Original Martín Fierro — English Reader Guide" description="English introduction and navigation to the complete original Spanish poem: two parts, 46 cantos and 7,210 source verses.">
<article class="reader-guide"><nav><a href="/en/">English edition</a> / Original poem guide</nav><p class="eyebrow">PRIMARY SOURCE · ENGLISH READER ORIENTATION</p><h1>Read Martín Fierro in the original Spanish</h1><p class="lead">José Hernández's poem consists of two books, published in 1872 and 1879, with 46 cantos in all. This English guide helps you navigate the site's original Spanish reader while keeping the source text unchanged.</p><div class="note"><strong>Language notice:</strong> The links labeled “Read original” lead to the Spanish poem, not an English translation. For explanations in English, choose “English study guide.”</div>
<p><a href="/en/verse-search/">Search all 7,210 original verses</a> · <a href="/en/students/">Browse English lessons</a> · <a href="/en/martin-fierro-english-translation/">Learn about English translations</a></p>
{parts.map(x=><section><h2>{x.title}</h2><p>{x.desc}</p><div class="cantos">{Array.from({length:x.total},(_,i)=>i+1).map(n=><article><strong>Canto {n}</strong><a href={`/en/students/${x.part==='ida'?'canto':'vuelta-canto'}-${n}/`}>English study guide</a><a href={`/leer/${x.part}/${n}/`} lang="es">Read original (Spanish)</a></article>)}</div></section>)}
<section><h2>How to cite a passage</h2><p>Identify the author, original book title, publication year, canto and stanza, using the displayed stanza number in the reader. Link to the permanent canto and stanza anchor when available. The English study headings are editorial and should not be cited as original poem titles.</p><p>The site uses a single structured source corpus shared by the reader, search and editorial commentary. No complete English translation is reproduced here. For textual variants or historical publication details, consult the <a href="/en/archive/">documentary archive</a>.</p></section></article>
